ween $75,000 and $122,000 per patient per year, excluding other medical expenses.SATISFACCI√ìN:Satisfaction is the degree to which patients feel their expectations regarding healthcare services are met.DONABEDIAN:Donabedian is considered the father of healthcare quality and proposed a framework for measuring healthcare quality through structure, process, and outcomes.AENOR:AENOR is the Spanish Association for Standardization and Certification, responsible for developing quality standards.ISO:ISO is the International Organization for Standardization, which develops and publishes international standards.UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2008:UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2008 is a quality management standard that was commonly used before being replaced by UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015.UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015:UNE-EN-ISO 9001:2015 is the updated quality management standard that became mandatory in 2017.DIMENSIONES DE CALIDAD:"Dimensiones de calidad" refers to the criteria and various aspects used to evaluate the quality of healthcare services. This concept encompasses multiple dimensions, including structure, process, and outcome dimensions, as well as accessibility, adequacy, and effectiveness. Together, these dimensions provide a comprehensive framework for assessing the overall quality of healthcare delivery.ESTRUCTURA:Estructura refers to the characteristics of the environment in which healthcare is provided, including the necessary resources.PROCESO:Proceso refers to the utilization of resources in the delivery of healthcare services, which can be related to both patients and organizations.RESULTADOS:Resultados refer to the effects of healthcare interventions on individuals or society, including both intermediate and final outcomes.CALIDAD SANITARIA:EUROPEAN FOUNDATION FOR QUALITY MANAGEMENT:The European Foundation for Quality Management (EFQM) is an organization that provides a model for excellence in management, particularly in healthcare systems.JOINT COMMISSION:The Joint Commission is an external committee that evaluates healthcare organizations to ensure they meet certain standards.QUALITY MANAGEMENT:Quality management refers to the processes and practices that organizations implement to ensure they meet quality standards and satisfy stakeholders.BENCHMARKING:Benchmarking is a systematic technique used by organizations to compare their processes with those of similar organizations to identify best practices.NUTRICI√ìN THERAPY:SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE CALIDAD ASISTENCIAL:The Sociedad Espa√±ola de Calidad Asistencial is an organization that collaborates in defining quality criteria for healthcare services.CULTURA DE SEGURIDAD:A safety culture in healthcare emphasizes the importance of safety and risk management practices among healthcare professionals.GESTI√ìN DE RIESGOS:Risk management involves identifying and analyzing potential risks in healthcare to propose solutions for minimizing them.ENCUESTAS:Surveys are tools used to measure patient satisfaction and gather feedback on healthcare services.LISTAS DE ESPERA:Waiting lists refer to the delays patients experience in receiving healthcare services, which can impact satisfaction.RETRASOS EN LA ATENCI√ìN:Delays in care refer to the time patients wait to receive medical attention or results, affecting their overall experience.COORDINACI√ìN ENTRE PROFESIONALES:Coordination among healthcare professionals is essential for providing seamless patient care and improving satisfaction.CRITERIOS DE CALIDAD:√ÅLVAREZ J:√Ålvarez J is an author who contributed to the study of clinical nutrition management and quality indicators in healthcare.MONEREO S:Monereo S is an author involved in the research on clinical nutrition management.ORTIZ P:Ortiz P is an author who co-authored works on clinical nutrition management.SALIDO S:Salido S is an author who contributed to the research on clinical nutrition management.LAUPACIS A:Laupacis A is an author who assessed clinically useful measures of treatment consequences.SACKETT DL:Sackett DL is a key contributor to the development of Evidence-Based Medicine and is recognized as an author who has written extensively on the subject. His work has significantly influenced the field, highlighting the importance of integrating clinical expertise with the best available evidence to improve patient care.ROBERTS:Roberts is an author who co-authored a study on clinically useful measures of treatment consequences.DEL LLANO JE:Del Llano JE is an author who wrote about cost-effective medicine and evidence-based medicine.OLIVA J:Oliva J is an author who contributed to the discussion on cost-effective medicine.INSTITUTO DE INFORMACI√ìN SANITARIA:The Instituto de Informaci√≥n Sanitaria is an organization that analyzes accounting systems in public hospitals in Spain.COPENHAGEN:Copenhagen is the capital of Denmark, where a WHO meeting on quality assurance principles was held.AN√ÅLISIS CAUSA-RA√çZ:An√°lisis causa-ra√≠z is a method used to identify the underlying causes of problems in healthcare processes.DIAGRAMA DE PARETO:Diagrama de Pareto is a statistical tool used to prioritize issues based on their impact in healthcare quality management.T√âCNICA DE LOS 5 PORQU√âS:T√©cnica de los 5 porqu√©s is a problem-solving technique used to explore the cause-and-effect relationships underlying a particular problem in healthcare.DIAGRAMA CAUSA-EFECTO:Diagrama causa-efecto, also known as the fishbone diagram, is a visual tool used to identify potential causes of a problem in healthcare quality management.SISTEMAS SANITARIOS P√öBLICOS Y PRIVADOS:Sistemas sanitarios p√∫blicos y privados refer to the healthcare systems that face challenges in improving performance and ensuring safety in medical procedures.PROCEDIMIENTOS ADECUADOS:Procedimientos adecuados refer to the necessary protocols implemented in healthcare to minimize risks associated with medical procedures.CALIDAD EN NUESTROS SERVICIOS:Calidad en nuestros servicios refers to the quality standards that healthcare services aim to achieve for better patient outcomes.VEGENAT, S.A.:VEGENAT, S.A. is a company involved in the research and development of clinical nutrition products, focusing on innovation and quality management.MILAGROS P√âREZ RODR√çGUEZ:Milagros P√©rez Rodr√≠guez is the Director of R&D and Quality at VEGENAT, S.A., overseeing the development of clinical nutrition products.√ÅFRICA JIM√âNEZ JIM√âNEZ:√Åfrica Jim√©nez Jim√©nez is the R&D Manager at VEGENAT, S.A., responsible for the research and development of nutrition products.ESCUELA NACIONAL DE SANIDAD:Escuela Nacional de Sanidad is an institution in Madrid dedicated to public health education and training, providing resources and research in the field.I+D:I+D, or Research and Development, is a systematic process crucial for innovation in the nutrition industry, as highlighted in the text.TERCERA EDICI√ìN:Tercera edici√≥n refers to the third edition of the text on clinical nutrition, indicating its updated content and relevance in the field.)<|COMPLETE|>VIGILANCIA TECNOL√ìGICA:La vigilancia tecnol√≥gica es una herramienta que permite captar y analizar informaci√≥n sobre ciencia y tecnolog√≠a para convertirla en conocimiento √∫til para la organizaci√≥n.INTELIGENCIA COMPETITIVA:La inteligencia competitiva es un enfoque que sustituye a la vigilancia tecnol√≥gica, a√±adiendo una dimensi√≥n estrat√©gica para anticipar tendencias.CREATIVIDAD:La creatividad es un proceso mental que ayuda a generar nuevas ideas y puede ser gestionada mediante t√©cnicas como mapas mentales y lluvia de ideas.AN√ÅLISIS DE SITUACI√ìN:El an√°lisis de situaci√≥n externa e interna es crucial para identificar casos de √©xito o fracaso en el mercado y evaluar las capacidades internas de la organizaci√≥n.EVALUACI√ìN DE OPORTUNIDADES:La evaluaci√≥n de oportunidades implica valorar la viabilidad t√©cnica, econ√≥mica y comercial de los proyectos de innovaci√≥n.DISE√ëO Y DESARROLLO DE PRODUCTOS:El dise√±o y desarrollo de productos es la fase pr√°ctica del proceso de innovaci√≥n que puede llevar de 6 meses a varios a√±os.MEMORIA DE PROYECTO:La memoria de proyecto es un documento que incluye los objetivos, la estrategia, el grado de innovaci√≥n y la planificaci√≥n de un nuevo proyecto.SISTEMA DE CALIDAD:El sistema de calidad de la organizaci√≥n es un marco que asegura que los nuevos proyectos se integren adecuadamente en los procesos existentes.PROYECTOS DE I+D+I:I+D+I:The entity "I+D+I" refers to the department responsible for research and development (I+D+i) of new products. This department evaluates the viability of these products and stays updated on the latest technical and technological advancements.AENE:AENE es la Asociaci√≥n Espa√±ola de Nutrici√≥n Enteral y Parenteral, que promueve la investigaci√≥n y desarrollo en el campo de la nutrici√≥n cl√≠nica.PRODUCTO DE NUTRICI√ìN CL√çNICA:REGLAMENTO (UE) N¬∫ 1924/2006:Reglamento (UE) N¬∫ 1924/2006 establece las normas sobre declaraciones nutricionales y de propiedades saludables en los alimentos.REGLAMENTO (UE) N¬∫ 1333/2008:Reglamento (UE) N¬∫ 1333/2008 establece una lista de aditivos alimentarios permitidos en la Uni√≥n Europea.REGLAMENTO (UE) N¬∫ 609/2013:Reglamento (UE) N¬∫ 609/2013 regula los alimentos destinados a lactantes y ni√±os de corta edad, as√≠ como los alimentos para usos m√©dicos especiales.REGLAMENTO DELEGADO (UE) N¬∫ 2016/128:Reglamento delegado (UE) N¬∫ 2016/128 establece requisitos espec√≠ficos de composici√≥n e informaci√≥n para alimentos m√©dicos especiales.REGLAMENTO (UE) N¬∫ 2016/1413:Reglamento (UE) N¬∫ 2016/1413 establece una lista de declaraciones autorizadas de propiedades saludables de los alimentos.BASES DE DATOS ESPECIALIZADAS:Las bases de datos especializadas son recursos que contienen informaci√≥n sobre ingredientes y productos alimenticios para su evaluaci√≥n.EVIDENCIA:EVIDENCIA refers to the data and findings that inform clinical decisions and practices, particularly in the field of nutrition. It encompasses the information and research findings that support clinical practices and guidelines, highlighting the effectiveness of various products and practices in nutrition. This comprehensive understanding of evidence is crucial for ensuring that clinical decisions are based on reliable and validated data.OGM:Los organismos gen√©ticamente modificados (OGM) son organismos cuyo material gen√©tico ha sido alterado de una manera que no ocurre naturalmente.DOCUMENTACI√ìN:La documentaci√≥n se refiere a los registros y documentos que acompa√±an a los ingredientes y productos alimenticios, asegurando su calidad y seguridad.FICHA DE DATOS DE SEGURIDAD (FDS):La Ficha de Datos de Seguridad es un documento que proporciona informaci√≥n sobre la seguridad y manejo de sustancias qu√≠micas en productos alimenticios.DIAGRAMA DE FLUJO DEL PROCESO:The "DIAGRAMA DE FLUJO DEL PROCESO" is a visual representation that outlines the various stages involved in the manufacturing of food products.SISTEMA APPCC:El Sistema APPCC (An√°lisis de Peligros y Puntos de Control Cr√≠ticos) es un enfoque sistem√°tico para la seguridad alimentaria que identifica y controla peligros en la producci√≥n de alimentos.)<|COMPLETE|>ISO 9001:ISO 9001 is a certification that ensures a product, process, or service meets specified requirements.ISO 14001:ISO 14001 is a certification that specifies requirements for an effective environmental management system.BRC:BRC (British Retail Consortium) is a certification that ensures the safety, quality, and operational criteria of food manufacturers.IFS:IFS (International Featured Standards) is a certification that ensures the safety and quality of products in the food industry.HALAL:Halal certification ensures that products meet Islamic dietary laws.KOSHER:Kosher certification ensures that food products comply with Jewish dietary laws.NUTRITIONAL PRODUCTS:Nutritional products are specifically developed to ensure the quality and adequacy of their ingredients for clinical nutrition. They encompass a diverse range of items aimed at supporting health and meeting dietary requirements. Notably, these products include offerings from well-known manufacturers such as Abbott and Fresenius Kabi, highlighting the industry's commitment to providing effective nutritional solutions.MINERALS AND VITAMINS:Minerals and vitamins are regulated and their amounts may vary based on the intended use of the nutritional product.AN√ÅLISIS DE PELIGROS Y PUNTOS DE CONTROL CR√çTICOS:The analysis of hazards and controls associated with risks in the manufacturing process.ESTUDIO BIOLOGICO DE BIODISPONIBILIDAD PROTEICA:A biological study assessing the digestibility and nutritional value of protein sources.VALOR DE DEXTROSA EQUIVALENTE:A measure indicating the degree of hydrolysis of starch molecules in carbohydrates.RELACI√ìN DE √ÅCIDOS GRASOS:The evaluation of the ratio of unsaturated to saturated fatty acids in lipids.RESISTENCIA A LA OXIDACI√ìN:The ability of fats to resist rancidity and oxidation during storage and use.RECOMENDACIONES DE USO:Guidelines that dictate the appropriate use of ingredients in nutritional products.COMPONENTES PROTEICOS:The various protein sources selected for their nutritional and functional properties.REGULAMENTO (UE) N¬∫ 609/2013:EU regulation that sets out the requirements for food intended for specific groups, including nutritional products.REGULAMENTO DELEGADO (UE) N¬∫ 2016/128:EU regulation that specifies requirements for food for special medical purposes.MALTODEXTRINA M:Maltodextrin M is a carbohydrate used in clinical nutrition formulations to provide energy and improve texture.PROTE√çNAS DE LA LECHE P:Milk proteins P are included in clinical nutrition products for their nutritional value and role in muscle maintenance.ACEITE VEGETAL V1:Vegetable oil V1 is used in formulations to provide essential fatty acids and improve palatability.ACEITE VEGETAL V2:Vegetable oil V2 serves a similar purpose as V1, contributing to the nutritional profile of the product.EMULGENTE E:Emulsifier E is used to stabilize mixtures of oil and water in clinical nutrition products.MEZCLA DE MINERALES:Mineral mix is included to ensure the product meets dietary mineral requirements.MEZCLA DE VITAMINAS:Vitamin mix is added to provide essential vitamins necessary for health.AROMA A:Flavoring A is used to enhance the taste of clinical nutrition products.EDULCORANTE E1:Sweetener E1 is used to improve the sweetness of the product without adding calories.ESTABILIZANTE EA:Stabilizer EA is used to maintain the consistency and texture of the product.ENSAYOS DE FORMULACI√ìN:Formulation trials are conducted to test the stability, viscosity, and sensory properties of the product.RECETA:A recipe is a detailed guide that outlines the specific ingredients and their quantities for creating a clinical nutrition product.AGENTES EMULSIONANTES:Emulsifying agents such as proteins or emulsifiers are used to stabilize emulsions in clinical nutrition products.HOMOGENEIZACI√ìN:Homogenization is a process applied to liquids to reduce particle size and create a uniform product, crucial in the formulation of clinical nutrition products.MEZCLA:Mezcla refers to the mixing process of ingredients in clinical nutrition, which is crucial for achieving the desired consistency and stability.PRODUCTO FINAL:Producto final refers to the end product of clinical nutrition formulations, which must meet specific quality and stability standards.PART√çCULAS:Part√≠culas refer to the small components in mixtures that can affect the overall stability and quality of clinical nutrition products.ESTABILIDAD:Estabilidad refers to the ability of a product to maintain its intended physical and chemical properties over time.GRANO:HOMOGENEIZADOR:HOMOGENEIZADOR is a device used in the process of mixing and stabilizing ingredients in clinical nutrition products.INTERACCIONES ENTRE INGREDIENTES:INTERACCIONES ENTRE INGREDIENTES refers to the interactions that occur between different components in clinical nutrition formulas, affecting their stability and effectiveness.DESNATURALIZACI√ìN:DESNATURALIZACI√ìN is the process by which proteins lose their natural structure due to factors like temperature, impacting their functionality in nutrition products.AGREGACI√ìN:AGREGACI√ìN refers to the clumping of denatured proteins, which can affect the quality of clinical nutrition products.PRECIPITACI√ìN:PRECIPITACI√ìN is the process where proteins settle out of solution, which can occur in clinical nutrition products under certain conditions.F√ìRMULAS DE NUTRICI√ìN CL√çNICA:MAILLARD REACTION:The Maillard reaction is a chemical reaction between amino acids and reducing sugars that gives browned food its distinctive flavor, which can affect the quality of clinical nutrition products.PRODUCTO:The PRODUCTO refers to the clinical nutrition items being developed, which are designed to maintain both organoleptic and nutritional quality. This product represents the final output of a comprehensive design and development process in clinical nutrition, undergoing various stages of testing and validation prior to its market launch.ALMACENAMIENTO:Storage refers to the conditions under which clinical nutrition products are kept, which can affect their quality and nutrient stability over time.SENSACI√ìN TRIGEMINAL:Trigeminal sensation refers to the mouthfeel experienced when consuming clinical nutrition products, which can be affected by protein coagulation and viscosity.TRATAMIENTO T√âRMICO:ICIDCA:ICIDCA is an organization involved in the scientific and industrial development of products, particularly in the context of scaling processes from laboratory to industrial production.PHOSPHATE STABILITY TEST:The phosphate stability test involves subjecting a product to an acidic environment and heat to determine its stability and coagulation properties.MICROBIOLOGICAL CONTROLS:Microbiological controls are evaluations conducted to confirm the effectiveness of thermal treatment in ensuring product sterility and safety.PHYSICAL-CHEMICAL CONTROLS:Physical-chemical controls are measures taken during product development to assess various attributes such as pH, viscosity, and particle size distribution.SENSORY EVALUATION:Sensory evaluation involves internal tastings to assess and select samples based on their organoleptic properties like color, odor, flavor, and texture.LABORATORY SCALE:Laboratory scale refers to the initial phase of product development where experiments are conducted to achieve desired results before scaling up.SEMI-INDUSTRIAL SCALE:Semi-industrial scale is the phase where the laboratory protocol is reproduced in a production plant at a larger volume than laboratory scale.INDUSTRIAL SCALE:Industrial scale is the final phase of production where the product is manufactured at full capacity based on successful laboratory and semi-industrial results.REGLAMENTO (UE) 1169/2011:Reglamento (UE) 1169/2011 is the European regulation that mandates the inclusion of food information for consumers, including the minimum durability date of food products.ESCALA LABORATORIO:Escala laboratorio is the initial stage of product development where prototypes are created and tested in a controlled environment.ESCALA SEMIINDUSTRIAL:Escala semiindustrial is the stage where the laboratory protocol is reproduced on a larger scale to assess feasibility and performance in production conditions.ESTUDIOS DE VIDA √öTIL:Estudios de vida √∫til are studies conducted to determine the shelf life of a product, ensuring it maintains its properties over time.PROTOTIPO:Prototipo is the initial model created during the design phase, which is tested and refined before moving to larger scale production.CONDICIONES NORMALES:Condiciones normales refers to the standard operating conditions under which the product is expected to perform during regular production.PLANTA DE PRODUCCI√ìN:COMIT√âS DE √âTICA:Ethics Committees that approve study protocols in accordance with legal regulationsLEY 14/2007:Law that governs the ethical approval of clinical studies in the context of nutritionREAL DECRETO 223/2004:Royal Decree that outlines the methodology for conducting clinical trialsPRODUCTOS DE NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL:Enteral nutrition products that are evaluated through clinical trialsPATENTES:The process of patenting products or processes in the field of nutritionAN√ÅLISIS DE VISCOSIDAD:Viscosity analysis is important for assessing the quality of enteral nutrition productsAN√ÅLISIS DE VITAMINAS:Vitamin analysis is conducted to ensure the nutritional adequacy of enteral nutrition productsAN√ÅLISIS ORGANOL√âPTICO:Organoleptic analysis evaluates the sensory attributes of enteral nutrition productsDISE√ëO DEL ESTUDIO:PRODUCTO ENTERAL:Alimento dise√±ado para usos m√©dicos especiales que requiere un registro espec√≠fico para su comercializaci√≥nDOSSER DEL PRODUCTO:Documento que recopila toda la informaci√≥n relativa a un producto de nutrici√≥n cl√≠nica, incluyendo ingredientes, procesado y evaluaciones cl√≠nicasCONGRESOS:Eventos donde se presentan y discuten investigaciones y resultados en el campo de la nutrici√≥n y la saludPUBLICACIONES:PUBLICACIONES refer to articles and studies that are published in scientific journals to communicate research findings in the field of nutrition. These publications serve as a vital means of disseminating knowledge and advancements in nutritional science to the broader academic and professional community.DIETAS EST√ÅNDAR:Tipos de dietas que pueden ser financiadas por el Sistema Nacional de Salud, no espec√≠ficas para patolog√≠asDIETAS DESTINADAS A PATOLOG√çAS ESPEC√çFICAS:Dietas que requieren evidencia adicional para su inclusi√≥n en el Sistema Nacional de Salud, enfocadas en condiciones m√©dicas particularesADMINISTRACI√ìN REGIONAL:FUNDACI√ìN COTEC:Fundaci√≥n Cotec para la Innovaci√≥n Tecnol√≥gica is an organization focused on technological innovation and research in Spain.OECD:The Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) is an intergovernmental economic organization with 38 member countries, founded in 1961 to stimulate economic progress and world trade.HOSPITAL CL√çNICO UNIVERSITARIO DE VALENCIA:Hospital Cl√≠nico Universitario de Valencia is a university hospital in Valencia, Spain, known for its clinical nutrition and dietetics programs.UNIVERSIDAD DE CANTABRIA:Universidad de Cantabria is a public university located in Santander, Spain, offering various academic programs and research opportunities.UE:The European Union (UE) is a political and economic union of 27 European countries that are located primarily in Europe.COTEC:COTEC is an abbreviation for Fundaci√≥n Cotec para la Innovaci√≥n Tecnol√≥gica, which promotes technological innovation in Spain.MINISTERIO PARA LA PRESIDENCIA Y PARA LAS ADMINISTRACIONES TERRITORIALES:The Ministry for the Presidency and Territorial Administrations is a governmental body in Spain responsible for various administrative functions.UNIVERSIDAD NACIONAL ABIERTA Y A DISTANCIA:A distance learning university in Colombia that offers various courses, including food chemistry and analysis.TETRA PAK:Tetra Pak is a multinational food processing and packaging company known for its innovative packaging solutions.CENGAGE LEARNING:Cengage Learning is an educational content, technology, and services company for the higher education and K-12 markets.EDICIONES MUNDI-PRENSA:Ediciones Mundi-Prensa is a publishing house that specializes in various educational and professional publications.CRC PRESS:CRC Press is a global publisher of scientific and technical research in various fields, including food engineering.FOOD CONTROL:A scientific journal that publishes research related to food safety, quality, and control measures.OFICINA ESPA√ëOLA DE PATENTES Y MARCAS:The Spanish Patent and Trademark Office is responsible for the registration and protection of intellectual property in Spain.ANA HERN√ÅNDEZ MORENO:Ana Hern√°ndez Moreno is a professional associated with the Servicio de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario in Le√≥n, contributing to evidence-based nutrition practices.EVIDENCE BASED MEDICINE:Evidence Based Medicine (EBM) is a medical practice model that emphasizes the integration of the best available research evidence with clinical expertise and patient values in making decisions about the care of individual patients. It represents a systematic approach to clinical problem-solving, ensuring that healthcare decisions are informed by current best evidence, thereby enhancing the quality of patient care.DAVID SACKETT:David Sackett is a key figure in the development of Evidence Based Medicine, advocating for the integration of clinical expertise with the best available evidence.GORDON GUYATT:Gordon Guyatt is a key figure in the development of Evidence Based Medicine, advocating for the integration of clinical expertise with the best available evidence.GROL:Grol es un investigador que calcul√≥ que un internista necesitar√≠a leer 20 art√≠culos diarios para mantenerse actualizado en su conocimiento m√©dico.GUYATT G:Guyatt G es un autor mencionado en relaci√≥n con las habilidades necesarias para una pr√°ctica cl√≠nica √≥ptima basada en la evidencia.EVIDENCIA CL√çNICA:La evidencia cl√≠nica se refiere a la informaci√≥n y datos obtenidos de investigaciones que son relevantes para la pr√°ctica m√©dica.PRACTICA CL√çNICA:La pr√°ctica cl√≠nica es el proceso de atenci√≥n m√©dica que se basa en la evidencia y la experiencia del m√©dico para tomar decisiones sobre el tratamiento de los pacientes.LIMITACIONES DE LA MBE:Las limitaciones de la Medicina Basada en la Evidencia incluyen la resistencia al cambio por parte de los cl√≠nicos y la dificultad de mantenerse actualizado con la gran cantidad de informaci√≥n m√©dica disponible.NUTRICI√ìN BASADA EN LA EVIDENCIA:"NUTRICI√ìN BASADA EN LA EVIDENCIA" refers to an approach that integrates the principles of evidence-based medicine (EBM) into the fields of nutrition and dietary practices. This methodology, also known as Nutrition based on Evidence (NuBE), emphasizes the application of the best available scientific evidence to inform clinical nutrition practices and community nutrition recommendations. By prioritizing scientific research and data, this approach aims to enhance the effectiveness and reliability of dietary recommendations and practices, ensuring that they are grounded in solid evidence.HABILIDADES:Las habilidades necesarias para una pr√°ctica cl√≠nica √≥ptima incluyen la b√∫squeda eficiente de informaci√≥n y el abordaje cr√≠tico de la literatura m√©dica.EXPERIENCIA CL√çNICA:La experiencia cl√≠nica es el conocimiento y la pr√°ctica acumulada por los m√©dicos a lo largo de su carrera, que se integra en la toma de decisiones m√©dicas.SENSIBILIDAD Y HABILIDADES DE COMUNICACI√ìN:La sensibilidad y habilidades de comunicaci√≥n son esenciales para comprender el contexto del paciente y sus necesidades en la atenci√≥n m√©dica.EVIDENCIA DE CALIDAD:La evidencia de calidad se refiere a la validez y relevancia de los datos utilizados en la pr√°ctica cl√≠nica, que son fundamentales para la toma de decisiones informadas.SACKETT:Sackett is a key figure in the development of evidence-based medicine, contributing to the creation of clinical guidelinesSTRAUSS:Strauss is involved in the ongoing development and editing of clinical guidelines related to evidence-based medicinePICO:PICO is a strategy used in evidence-based medicine to formulate clinical questions regarding patients, interventions, controls, and outcomesPOEM:POEM stands for Patient Oriented Evidence that Matters, focusing on evidence that is relevant to patient outcomesGU√çAS DE PR√ÅCTICA CL√çNICA:GU√çAS DE PR√ÅCTICA CL√çNICA are structured recommendations designed to enhance patient care by utilizing the best available evidence. These guidelines serve as evidence-based recommendations that assist healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding patient treatment and management.LITERATURA M√âDICA:BMJ CLINICAL EVIDENCE:BMJ Clinical Evidence is an online resource providing updated summaries of integrated evidence for clinical practice.DYNAMED:DynaMed is a clinical decision support tool that offers evidence-based information to healthcare providers.INFORETRIEVER:InfoRetriever is an online tool designed to help healthcare professionals find relevant clinical information quickly.FISTERRA:Fisterra is a medical resource providing evidence-based information and guidelines for healthcare professionals in Spanish-speaking countries.COCHRANE COLLABORATION:The Cochrane Collaboration publishes systematic reviews and clinical trials to provide high-quality evidence for healthcare decision-making.MEDLINE:MEDLINE is a widely used bibliographic database of life sciences and biomedical information, accessible via the internet.EMBASE:Embase is a biomedical and pharmacological database of published literature, providing comprehensive coverage of drug and medical research.WEB OF SCIENCE:Web of Science is an online subscription-based scientific citation indexing service that provides comprehensive citation data for various academic disciplines.TRIPDATABASE:TRIPdatabase is a clinical search engine designed to provide evidence-based information for healthcare professionals.GOOGLE:Google is a widely used search engine that can also be utilized to find medical information, though not always critically evaluated.PIR√ÅMIDE DE FUENTES DE INFORMACI√ìN:The Pir√°mide de Fuentes de Informaci√≥n is a model that illustrates the hierarchy of medical information sources, guiding healthcare professionals in their search for evidence-based resources.BIBLIOTECA COCHRANE:The Biblioteca Cochrane is a collection of systematic reviews and clinical trials published by the Cochrane Collaboration, providing high-quality evidence for healthcare decisions.PUBMED CLINICAL QUERIES:PubMed Clinical Queries is a tool that allows users to search for systematic reviews and clinical studies within the PubMed database.HAYNES:AMERICAN DIETETICS ASSOCIATION:The American Dietetics Association (ADA) defines the practice of evidence-based nutrition as the use of systematically reviewed scientific evidence to make practical decisions about food and nutrition.UNIVERSITY OF TORONTO:The University of Toronto provides resources for critical appraisal and evidence-based medicine practices.CENTRE FOR EVIDENCE BASED MEDICINE:The Centre for Evidence Based Medicine, located in Oxford, is dedicated to enhancing clinical practice through the provision of classifications of scientific evidence types for clinical practice guidelines. Additionally, the Centre offers various tools designed to evaluate evidence and improve clinical decision-making, thereby supporting healthcare professionals in making informed choices based on the best available evidence.CRITICAL APPRAISAL OF THE EVIDENCE:Critical Appraisal of the Evidence is a program at the University of Toronto that focuses on evaluating medical literature.EVIDENCE BASED MEDICINE TOOL KIT:The Evidence Based Medicine Tool Kit at the University of Alberta offers resources for implementing evidence-based practices in clinical settings.RED CASPE:Red CASPe is a network that provides training in critical reading skills for evaluating medical literature.NUTRICI√ìN COMUNITARIA:NUTRICI√ìN COMUNITARIA, or community nutrition, refers to the application of nutrition principles and practices aimed at improving the health of populations. This field encompasses efforts to enhance community health through proper dietary practices and nutritional education. It emphasizes the importance of food and nutrition in fostering better health outcomes within communities.USERS' GUIDES INTERACTIVE:INDUSTRIA FARMAC√âUTICA:La industria farmac√©utica financia la mayor parte de la investigaci√≥n cl√≠nica, lo que puede introducir sesgos en los resultados de los estudios.SUPERALIMENTOS:Los superalimentos son alimentos que se promocionan como capaces de tratar o prevenir enfermedades, aunque su efectividad no siempre est√° respaldada por evidencia cient√≠fica.ESTUDIOS OBSERVACIONALES:Los estudios observacionales son investigaciones que pueden proporcionar evidencia sobre el efecto de las modificaciones diet√©ticas en la salud, aunque a menudo se consideran de menor calidad que los EPA.CANADIAN TASK FORCE:The Canadian Task Force is an institution that published a classification of levels of evidence and corresponding grades of recommendation for clinical practice guidelines.NATIONAL INSTITUTE FOR HEALTH AND CLINICAL EXCELLENCE:The National Institute for Health and Clinical Excellence (NICE) is an organization that plays a crucial role in enhancing health and social care in the UK. It provides national guidance and advice aimed at improving the quality of care and health outcomes. Additionally, NICE is responsible for developing clinical practice guidelines, which are structured with a hierarchical classification of evidence to ensure that recommendations are based on the best available data. Through its efforts, NICE seeks to promote effective and efficient healthcare practices across the nation.GRADE:GRADE is a system designed for grading the quality of evidence and the strength of recommendations in clinical practice guidelines. Known as the Grading of Recommendations, Assessment, Development, and Evaluations, the GRADE system aims to establish a common language for discussing the quality of evidence and the strength of recommendations within clinical practice guidelines.EVIDENCE BASED NUTRITION GUIDELINES:Evidence-based nutrition guidelines are documents that include recommendations to optimize patient care based on systematic reviews of evidence.CLINICAL PRACTICE GUIDELINES:Clinical practice guidelines (GPC) are informative documents that include recommendations aimed at optimizing patient care based on systematic reviews of evidence.EVIDENCE CLASSIFICATION SYSTEMS:Evidence classification systems are frameworks used to categorize studies based on scientific rigor and reliability.EVIDENCE:Evidence refers to the information and data collected through research that supports clinical practice guidelines and recommendations.RIGOR SCIENTIFIC:Rigor scientific refers to the strictness and precision in the design of studies, which is crucial for determining the quality of evidence in clinical practice guidelines.AGREE:AGREE is a collaboration initiated in 1998 among several countries aimed at improving the quality of clinical practice guidelines through methodological evaluation and transparency.GPC:Clinical Practice Guidelines (GPC) are structured recommendations aimed at improving patient care based on the best available evidence.INSTRUMENTO AGREE:The AGREE Instrument is a tool developed from the AGREE collaboration to assess the methodological rigor and transparency of clinical practice guidelines.CANADIAN CRITICAL CARE PRACTICE GUIDELINES:The Canadian Critical Care Practice Guidelines focus on nutritional support for critically ill patients and have been updated frequently since their first publication in 2003.NATIONAL INSTITUTE FOR CLINICAL EXCELLENCE:The National Institute for Clinical Excellence (NICE) provides guidelines for clinical practice in the UK, including those related to nutrition, with a history dating back to 2006.GORDON JENSEN:Gordon Jensen is a key figure involved in the development of common guidelines for nutritional management, collaborating with ESPEN and ASPEN.ALASTAIR FORBES:Alastair Forbes is another key figure who has worked with Gordon Jensen in the effort to create common guidelines for nutritional management.SIGN:SIGN is an organization that provides a classification system for evidence, which has been used in the development of clinical practice guidelines.MEDICINA BASADA EN PRUEBAS:Medicina basada en pruebas refers to evidence-based medicine, which aims to integrate clinical research with clinical expertise and patient values.EVIDENCE-BASED MEDICINE:Evidence-Based Medicine is a modern medical movement that emphasizes the use of evidence from well-designed and conducted research in healthcare decision-making.UNIVERSITY OF VIRGINIA HEALTH SYSTEM:The University of Virginia Health System is a healthcare provider that offers a range of medical services and is involved in medical education and research.ACTA INFORM MED:Acta Inform Med is a journal that publishes articles related to medical informatics and healthcare technology.EVIDENCE-BASED MEDICINE WORKING GROUP:The Evidence-Based Medicine Working Group is a collective of experts that promotes the principles and practices of evidence-based medicine.EVIDENCE-BASED MEDICINE PYRAMID:The Evidence-Based Medicine Pyramid is a framework for understanding the hierarchy of evidence in medical research.FERGUSON JH:Ferguson JH is a co-author of the analysis of the National Institutes of Health Medicare Coverage Assessment.GUYATT GH:Guyatt GH is a prominent figure in the field of Evidence-Based Medicine, known for his significant contributions to the development of the GRADE system. He has published extensively on evidence-based medicine and is recognized for authoring several key publications that have shaped the discipline.GLASZIOU P:Glasziou P is an author who has published works related to Evidence-Based Medicine and its impact on healthcare.HAYNES RB:Haynes RB is a researcher and author known for his contributions to Evidence-Based Medicine.RICHARDSON WS:Richardson WS is a co-author of significant works on Evidence-Based Medicine.ZIMERMAN AL:Zimerman AL is an author who has written about the history of Evidence-Based Medicine.MASIC I:Masic I is an author discussing new approaches and challenges in Evidence-Based Medicine.STRAUS SE:Straus SE is an editor and author involved in the publication of works on Evidence-Based Medicine.DUBINSKY M:CANADIAN TASK FORCE ON THE PERIODIC HEALTH EXAMINATION:The Canadian Task Force on the Periodic Health Examination is an organization that develops guidelines for preventive health care in Canada.GRADE WORKING GROUP:The GRADE Working Group is an international collaboration that develops a system for rating the quality of evidence and strength of recommendations in healthcare.FISTERRA.COM:Fisterra.com is a website that evaluates the quality of evidence and the grading of recommendations in clinical guidelines.KAVANAGH BP:Kavanagh BP is a researcher who has contributed to the development of the GRADE system for rating clinical guidelines.EVIDENCE ANALYSIS MANUAL:The Evidence Analysis Manual is a document published by the American Dietetic Association that provides guidelines for conducting evidence analysis in nutrition and dietetics.NUTRITION SUPPORT IN ADULTS:Nutrition support in adults refers to clinical guidelines developed by NICE for providing nutritional support through various methods including oral, enteral, and parenteral nutrition.AGREE II:AGREE II is a tool designed to enhance the quality of clinical practice guidelines by offering a structured framework for their development and reporting.EBHC PYRAMID 5.0:The EBHC Pyramid 5.0 is a model for accessing preappraised evidence and guidance in evidence-based healthcare.DISCREPANCIES IN NUTRITIONAL RECOMMENDATIONS:Discrepancies in nutritional recommendations refer to the variations and inconsistencies in dietary guidelines and advice provided by different organizations.HISTORY OF LEVELS OF EVIDENCE:The history of levels of evidence refers to the evolution of the classification system used to evaluate the quality of evidence in clinical research.EVIDENCE-BASED HEALTHCARE:AGREE TRUST:AGREE Trust is an organization focused on developing and improving clinical practice guidelines, particularly in the field of nutrition and health care.ANA URIOSTE FONDO:Ana Urioste Fondo is a medical professional working in the field of endocrinology and nutrition, contributing to the development of guidelines for artificial nutrition.INTERNATIONAL CONSENSUS GUIDELINE COMMITTEE PANCREATITIS TASK FORCE:This committee develops international consensus guidelines for nutrition therapy in pancreatitis, aiming to standardize care practices.PRODUCTOS DIET√âTICOS:Dietary products that are included in the offerings of the Sistema Nacional de Salud for medical use.ORDEN 2 JUNIO 1998:A legal order published on June 2, 1998, concerning home enteral nutrition in Spain.LEY 53/2002:A law enacted on December 30, 2002, addressing fiscal, administrative, and social measures in Spain.LEY 16/2003:A law enacted on May 28, 2003, focused on the cohesion and quality of the national health system in Spain.REAL DECRETO 1030/2006:A royal decree published on September 15, 2006, detailing the catalog of services offered by the national health system in Spain.ORDEN SCO/3858/2006:A legal order published on December 5, 2006, regulating home enteral nutrition formulas in Spain.ORDEN SPI/2958/2010:A legal order published on November 16, 2010, regarding the inclusion of special medical dietary foods in the national health system's offerings.REAL DECRETO-LEY 16/2012:A royal decree-law published on April 20, 2012, aimed at ensuring the sustainability of the national health system in Spain.ORDEN SSI/1640/2012:A legal order published on July 18, 2012, modifying the common service portfolio of the national health system in Spain.ORDEN SSI/2366/2012:A legal order published on October 30, 2012, concerning the billing of dietary products in Spain.ORDEN SSI/1329/2014:A legal order published on July 22, 2014, modifying the supplementary common portfolio of dietary products in Spain.ORDEN 30 ABRIL 1997:TUMORES DEL APARATO DIGESTIVO:Digestive system tumors, such as those in the esophagus and stomach, can cause severe swallowing issues requiring enteral nutrition.CIRUG√çA OTORRINOLARINGOL√ìGICA:Otorhinolaryngological surgery may result in complications that necessitate enteral nutrition for recovery.COMA NEUROL√ìGICO:Neurological coma can prevent normal eating, necessitating enteral nutrition support.S√çNDROMES DE MALABSORCI√ìN SEVERA:Severe malabsorption syndromes require enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake.ENFERMEDADES NEUROL√ìGICAS SUBSIDIARIAS:Certain neurological diseases may be treated with ketogenic diets, which can involve enteral nutrition.ALERGIA O INTOLERANCIA A LAS PROTE√çNAS DE LECHE DE VACA:Allergy or intolerance to cow's milk proteins in infants may require specialized enteral nutrition.PACIENTES CON ENCEFALOPAT√çA HEP√ÅTICA CR√ìNICA:Patients with chronic hepatic encephalopathy may need enteral nutrition due to dietary protein intolerance.)<|COMPLETE|>ARAG√ìN:Arag√≥n is an autonomous community in Spain where patients must submit a justification report from a hospital specialist to continue treatment for nutritional needs.BALEARES:Baleares is an autonomous community in Spain where patients must submit a justification report from a hospital specialist to continue treatment for nutritional needs.CANTABRIA:Cantabria is an autonomous community in Spain where patients must submit a justification report to continue treatment for nutritional needs.CASTILLA-LA MANCHA:Castilla-La Mancha is an autonomous community in Spain where patients must submit a justification report from a specialist to continue treatment for nutritional needs.LA RIOJA:La Rioja is an autonomous community in Spain where patients must submit a justification report to the corresponding Health Services Inspection to continue treatment for nutritional needs.PA√çS VASCO:Pa√≠s Vasco is an autonomous community in Spain where patients must submit a justification report to the nearest Health Services Inspection to continue treatment for nutritional needs.INGESA:INGESA is an organization responsible for health services in certain regions of Spain, where patients must submit a justification report to continue treatment for nutritional needs.PATOLOG√çA M√âDICA INFECCIOSA:Patoolog√≠a m√©dica infecciosa refers to infectious diseases that cause severe malabsorption, such as AIDS, leading to malnutrition.INSUFICIENCIA RENAL INFANTIL:Insuficiencia renal infantil is a condition that compromises the growth of the patient and can lead to malnutrition.NED:NED is a multifaceted entity that encompasses both a nutritional support program and a medical condition. As a nutritional support program, NED focuses on providing home care for elderly patients, specifically managing their nutritional needs to enhance their quality of life. Additionally, NED refers to a nutritional therapy designed for patients, particularly those suffering from gastrointestinal cancer, aimed at maintaining weight and improving overall quality of life. The term NED also stands for Nutrici√≥n Enteral Domiciliaria, which signifies enteral nutrition administered at home, with varying regulations and practices across different countries. Furthermore, NED has been studied epidemiologically as a medical condition in various countries, highlighting its significance in both clinical and nutritional contexts.SNS:SNS stands for Sistema Nacional de Salud, the national health system in Spain that includes provisions for NPD and NED.B√âLGICA:B√©lgica is Belgium, where patients may have to cover part of the costs for NED.POLONIA:Polonia refers to Poland, a country that is included in the epidemiological study of NED. In this context, patients in Poland may be required to cover a portion of the costs associated with NED.SUECIA:Suecia, which refers to Sweden, is identified as one of the eight countries that face limitations in data collection for epidemiological studies. Additionally, it is noted that Sweden has limited data on home nutrition, highlighting challenges in gathering comprehensive nutritional information within the country.REGULACI√ìN:Regulaci√≥n refers to the establishment of rules or laws governing the provision of NPD and NED, which varies by country.HOSPITALIZACI√ìN A DOMICILIO:Hospitalizaci√≥n a domicilio refers to home hospitalization services that may collaborate in the organization of NPD.COMPAN√çAS FARMAC√âUTICAS:Compa√±√≠as farmac√©uticas are pharmaceutical companies that may act as providers of NPD solutions.PROGRAMAS DE MEDICARE:Programas de Medicare are federal health insurance programs in the United States for individuals aged 65 and older or disabled, covering aspects of NED.PROGRAMAS DE MEDICAID:Programas de Medicaid are health insurance programs in the United States that provide coverage for low-income individuals, including aspects of NED.EE.UU.:EE.UU. is one of the eight countries mentioned that has limitations in data collection for epidemiological studies.BANS:BANS, which stands for the British Artificial Nutrition Survey, is a registry that focuses on estimating the prevalence of nutritional disorders in the UK. It has specifically published data regarding the prevalence of nutritional deficiencies (NED) and nutritional support (NPD). In 2011, BANS provided significant insights into the prevalence of NPD, contributing to the understanding of artificial nutrition needs within the British population.NADYA-SENPE:NADYA-SENPE is a specialized working group in Spain dedicated to home enteral nutrition. This group is responsible for maintaining various national registries that pertain to nutrition care, including annual registries of enteral and parenteral nutrition, which have been conducted since the late 1990s. Additionally, NADYA-SENPE is actively involved in research concerning health-related quality of life, particularly focusing on patients who receive home nutritional support. The group has also been collecting data on patients undergoing nutritional support therapy since 1992, specifically for those receiving NPD (Nutritional Parenteral Diet). Through these efforts, NADYA-SENPE plays a crucial role in advancing the understanding and management of nutritional care in Spain.NUTRICI√ìN ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA Y AMBULATORIA:The group of Artificial Nutrition Domiciliary and Ambulatory is involved in the study and registration of NED in Spain.BELGICA:OASIS:OASIS was a registry in the USA that recorded patients with NPD in 1987 before changing its name to the National Registry of Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition.SUSTAIN:SUSTAIN is A.S.P.E.N.'s National Patient Registry for Nutrition Care, specifically designed to focus on home parenteral nutrition outcomes. Established in 2011, SUSTAIN aims to include 100% of incident and prevalent patients with nutrition-related disorders (NPD). This comprehensive registry serves as a vital resource for tracking and improving the quality of nutrition care provided to patients receiving home parenteral nutrition.USA:The USA is a country where the OASIS registry was established to track patients with NPD.2014:The year 2014 is significant as it marks the last available data reporting 220 patients with NPD in the NADYA registry.2011:The year 2011 marks the creation of the Sustain system in the USA for tracking NPD patients.1993:The year 1993 is significant as it marks the year when the prevalence of NPD in Europe was reported to vary between 0.3 and 12.2 patients/million.1992:The year 1992 is significant as it marks the beginning of the NADYA registry's data collection on NPD patients.1994:The year 1994 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.1995:The year 1995 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.1996:The year 1996 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2000:The year 2000 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2001:The year 2001 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2002:The year 2002 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2003:The year 2003 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2004:The year 2004 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2005:The year 2005 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2006:The year 2006 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2007:The year 2007 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2008:The year 2008 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2009:The year 2009 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2010:The year 2010 is part of the timeline for the evolution of home parenteral nutrition as recorded in the NADYA registry.2011-2012:The period 2011-2012 is significant for the collection of data on NPD patients in the NADYA registry.2015:The year 2015 marks the final report of the Sustain system, which included 1,642 patients.32 CENTROS:The 32 centers that participated in the Sustain system for tracking NPD patients in the USA.IGLESIAS ROSADO C:Iglesias Rosado C is an author who contributed to the guidelines on home artificial nutrition for oncological patientsDE COS BLANCO AI:De Cos Blanco AI is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of home enteral nutrition in Spain. They have played a pivotal role in developing guidelines specifically focused on home artificial nutrition for oncological patients, showcasing their expertise and commitment to improving nutritional care for individuals undergoing cancer treatment.CASTILLO RABANEDA R:Castillo Rabaneda R is an author who contributed to the guidelines on home artificial nutrition for oncological patientsMATEO LOBO R:Mateo Lobo R is an author who contributed to the guidelines on home artificial nutrition for oncological patientsATENCI√ìN ESPECIALIZADA:Specialized care services that collaborate in the management of patients receiving home artificial nutritionNAD:NAD refers to nutritional support provided at home, specifically focusing on artificial nutrition administered in a home setting. This approach is being compared to standard treatment regarding its cost-effectiveness and the benefits it offers. Additionally, NAD has been studied in relation to the quality of life of both patients receiving this form of nutrition and their caregivers, highlighting its significance in improving overall well-being in a home care context.QOL-EF:El QOL-EF es un cuestionario espec√≠fico para evaluar la calidad de vida en pacientes con c√°ncer de cabeza y cuello que reciben nutrici√≥n enteral.NUTRIQOL:NutriQoL es un cuestionario que valora la calidad de vida en pacientes con nutrici√≥n enteral, independientemente de la v√≠a de administraci√≥n y la enfermedad.HIDRATACI√ìN ARTIFICIAL:La hidrataci√≥n artificial es un tema controvertido en el cuidado de pacientes al final de la vida, y su uso no siempre es recomendado.EORTC-QLQ-C30:EORTC-QLQ-C30 is a quality of life assessment tool used in cancer patients to measure the impact of treatments on their well-being.NI√ëOS CON NED:Children receiving NED are young patients who require nutritional support, with their caregivers experiencing psychological effects.S√çNDROME DEL CUIDADOR ¬´QUEMADO¬ª:Caregiver burnout syndrome is a condition characterized by physical, emotional, and mental exhaustion experienced by caregivers.PACIENTES CR√ìNICOS:Chronic patients are individuals with long-term health conditions who may require ongoing care and support.EUROS:Euros are the currency used in financial assessments related to the costs of nutritional support for patients in various studies.QALY:QALY, which stands for Quality-Adjusted Life Year, is a measure utilized in cost-utility analysis to evaluate the effectiveness of medical treatments, including home artificial nutrition. It assesses the value of medical interventions by considering both the quality and quantity of life they provide.ESTUDIO ESPA√ëOL DE 2007:A study conducted in Spain in 2007 that evaluated the costs associated with nutritional support for malnourished patients.COMPETENCIA DE NED:The competition faced by NED in providing nutritional support and the associated economic implications.MART√çNEZ MA:Mart√≠nez MA es uno de los autores que ha contribuido a la bibliograf√≠a sobre nutrici√≥n artificial domiciliaria.√ÅLVAREZ HERN√ÅNDEZ J:√Ålvarez Hern√°ndez J es uno de los autores que ha contribuido a la bibliograf√≠a sobre la utilizaci√≥n cl√≠nica de la nutrici√≥n enteral.NUTRICI√ìN ORAL DOMICILIARIA:La nutrici√≥n oral domiciliaria es un tipo de intervenci√≥n que se utiliza para complementar la alimentaci√≥n de pacientes en sus hogares.BRITISH ARTIFICIAL NUTRITION SURVEY:A committee of BAPEN that conducts annual reports on artificial nutrition support in the UK.NESTLE NUTRITION WORKSHOP:A series of workshops focused on clinical performance and nutrition, particularly enteral nutrition reimbursement.ANNUAL BANS REPORT:An annual report published by the British Artificial Nutrition Survey detailing the state of artificial nutrition support in the UK.SWITZERLAND:A country in Europe where home artificial nutrition practices were surveyed from 2005 to 2009.SHAFFER J:Shaffer J is an author who has co-written studies on home artificial nutrition and its clinical outcomes.PERTKIEWICZ M:Pertkiewicz M is a researcher who has co-authored studies on home artificial nutrition and its reimbursement policies.CASTELL√ì-BOT√çA I:Castell√≥-Bot√≠a I is an author who has conducted systematic reviews on artificial nutritional support registries.WANDEN-BERGHE C:Wanden-Berghe C is a researcher actively engaged in various reports and studies concerning nutritional practices in Spain and Europe. Specifically, Wanden-Berghe C has focused on home parenteral nutrition and home enteral nutrition, contributing to multiple studies and registries in these areas. Additionally, Wanden-Berghe C has made significant contributions to research on artificial nutrition practices across Europe, highlighting their expertise and involvement in the field of nutritional science.SANZ-VALERO C:Sanz-Valero C is an author involved in research related to artificial nutritional support and its implementation.CUERDA:Cuerda is an author mentioned in the context of home artificial nutrition research.MOROENO JM:SOCIETY GALLEGA DE NUTRICI√ìN Y DIET√âTICA:The Society Gallega de Nutrici√≥n y Diet√©tica is involved in nutrition and dietetics in Galicia, Spain, contributing to the field of nutrition care.CANADIAN HOME PARENTERAL NUTRITION REGISTRY:The Canadian HPN registry collects data on home parenteral nutrition in Canada, focusing on patient outcomes and validation.FR√çAS L:Fr√≠as L is a researcher involved in the documentation and studies of home enteral nutrition in Spain.CALA√ëAS A:Cala√±as A is a researcher who has contributed to the studies and registries of home enteral nutrition in Spain.GUENTER P:Guenter P is a contributor to the development of national patient registries for nutrition care.HEAPHEY L:Heaphey L is a researcher involved in the North American registry for home parenteral nutrition outcomes.FLEMING CR:Fleming CR is a researcher who has contributed to the North American registry for home parenteral nutrition.LININGER L:Lininger L is a researcher involved in the North American registry for home parenteral nutrition outcomes.STEIGER E:Steiger E is a researcher who has contributed to the North American registry for home parenteral nutrition outcomes.DI MARIA-GHALILI RA:Di Maria-Ghalili RA is a contributor to the development of national patient registries for nutrition care.ARMSTRONG D:Armstrong D is a researcher involved in the Canadian home parenteral nutrition registry.ALLARD JP:Allard JP is a researcher who has contributed to the Canadian home parenteral nutrition registry.MORNO JM:Moreno JM is a contributor to the NADYA group, involved in the documentation of home parenteral nutrition.NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL DOMICILIARIA EN ESPA√ëA:The annual reports on home parenteral nutrition in Spain, compiled by the Grupo NADYA-SENPE.CS:CS is a researcher involved in the development and validation of quality-of-life questionnaires for head and neck cancer patients.GAVAZZI C:Gavazzi C is a researcher who conducted a multicentre randomized clinical trial on the impact of home enteral nutrition in malnourished patients with upper gastrointestinal cancer.FARUQUIE SS:Faruquie SS is a researcher who evaluated patient quality of life and satisfaction with home enteral feeding and oral nutrition support services.WINKLER:Winkler is a researcher who reviewed the clinical, social, and economic impacts of home parenteral nutrition dependence in short bowel syndrome.HUISMAN-DE WAAL:Huisman-de Waal is a researcher who reviewed the impact of home parenteral nutrition on daily life.VASHI:Vashi is a researcher who conducted a longitudinal study on quality of life and nutritional outcomes in advanced cancer patients receiving home parenteral nutrition.IMSERSO:IMSERSO is an organization that published a white paper on the care of people in situations of dependency in Spain.CALDER√ìN:Calder√≥n is a researcher who studied the feelings of burden, psychological distress, and anxiety among primary caregivers of children with home enteral nutrition.JUDIK:Judik is a researcher who studied the difficulties, satisfactions, and support needs of caregivers assisting older patients with home enteral nutrition therapy.VILLAR:Villar is a researcher who conducted a descriptive study on home artificial nutrition in a sanitary area of Galicia, Spain.EDINGTON J:Edington J is a researcher who conducted a trial on nutritional supplementation in malnourished elderly individuals in the community.HOME ENTERAL NUTRITION:Home enteral nutrition refers to the medical practice of providing nutritional support to patients at home through enteral feeding methods.DEPENDENCY:Dependency refers to the condition of needing assistance with daily activities, often addressed in healthcare and social services.CROSS-SECTIONAL STUDY:A cross-sectional study is a type of observational research that analyzes data from a population at a specific point in time.MULTICENTRE RANDOMISED CLINICAL TRIAL:A multicentre randomized clinical trial is a study conducted across multiple locations to evaluate the effectiveness of a treatment.PHARMACO-ECONOMIC STUDY:A pharmaco-economic study assesses the cost-effectiveness of pharmaceutical interventions in healthcare.QUALITY OF LIFE QUESTIONNAIRE:A quality of life questionnaire is a tool used to measure patients' perceptions of their well-being and functional status.NUTRITION TEAM FOLLOW-UP:Nutrition team follow-up refers to ongoing support and assessment provided by a team of nutrition professionals to patients receiving nutritional therapy.)<|COMPLETE|>BEGO√ëA PINTOR DE LA MAZA:Bego√±a Pintor de la Maza is a researcher in clinical nutrition, affiliated with the Clinical Nutrition Unit at the University Hospital of Le√≥n.MIRIAM ALEJO RAMOS:Miriam Alejo Ramos is a researcher specializing in clinical nutrition, part of the Clinical Nutrition Unit at the University Hospital of Le√≥n.EPIDEMIOLOG√çA:Epidemiology is the study of how diseases affect the health and illness of populations, which is crucial for understanding nutritional health.DISEASE-RELATED MALNUTRITION:Disease-related malnutrition refers to nutritional deficiencies that occur as a result of illness, impacting patient recovery and health outcomes.CLINICAL NUTRITION UNIT:ESTUDIO EPIDEMIOL√ìGICO:El estudio epidemiol√≥gico es un proceso destinado a responder preguntas sobre la salud de una poblaci√≥n y evaluar la efectividad de intervenciones sanitarias.ESTUDIO DE COHORTES:El estudio de cohortes es un tipo de estudio anal√≠tico que eval√∫a la relaci√≥n entre la exposici√≥n a un factor y un resultado de salud en un grupo espec√≠fico a lo largo del tiempo.ESTUDIO CASOS-CONTROLES:El estudio casos-controles es un tipo de estudio anal√≠tico que compara individuos con una enfermedad (casos) con aquellos sin la enfermedad (controles) para identificar factores de riesgo.ESTUDIO ECOL√ìGICO:El estudio ecol√≥gico es un tipo de estudio observacional que analiza datos a nivel de poblaci√≥n para identificar patrones de salud y factores de riesgo.ESTUDIO TRANSVERSAL:"ESTUDIO TRANSVERSAL" refers to a type of study that is designed to describe the presence of a causal factor or disease within a population at a specific point in time. This method allows researchers to gather data and analyze the prevalence of certain conditions or characteristics without manipulating any variables, providing a snapshot of the situation being studied.ASPECTOS LEGALES:Los aspectos legales se refieren a las normativas y regulaciones que afectan la investigaci√≥n y la pr√°ctica en el √°mbito de la salud y la nutrici√≥n.ESTUDIOS EPIDEMIOL√ìGICOS:Los estudios epidemiol√≥gicos son investigaciones que buscan entender la salud de poblaciones y evaluar intervenciones sanitarias.VARIABLES:Las variables son factores que se miden y analizan en los estudios para determinar su relaci√≥n con la salud y la enfermedad.HIP√ìTESIS:La hip√≥tesis es una suposici√≥n que se pone a prueba en un estudio para determinar su validez en relaci√≥n con la salud.ENSAYO:Ensayo es un estudio que se utiliza para probar la eficacia de intervenciones terap√©uticas o preventivas y evaluar la causalidad de enfermedades.ESTUDIOS TRANSVERSALES:Estudios transversales son investigaciones que permiten estimar la prevalencia de una enfermedad en una poblaci√≥n espec√≠fica en un momento determinado.HISTORIA NATURAL DE LA ENFERMEDAD:Historia natural de la enfermedad se refiere al curso de una enfermedad en ausencia de intervenci√≥n m√©dica, √∫til para entender su evoluci√≥n.INCIDENCIA:Incidencia refers to the occurrence of new cases of a disease within a specified time frame. It is a crucial epidemiological measure that indicates the number of new cases in a population during a defined period. Notably, incidencias are not directly measured in case-control studies, which focus on existing cases rather than new occurrences.MORIANA ET AL:Moriana et al is a group of researchers who conducted a study in 2013 on nutritional assessment methods in a tertiary hospital.LOPEZ-ABENTE ET AL:L√≥pez-Abente et al is a group of researchers who conducted a study in 2012 relating colorectal cancer presence to pollution in cities.NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT STUDY:A study conducted by Moriana et al in 2013 to evaluate nutritional assessment methods and prevalence of malnutrition in a tertiary hospital.CANCER AND POLLUTION STUDY:A study conducted by L√≥pez-Abente et al in 2012 to investigate the relationship between colorectal cancer and pollution in cities.ESTUDIOS ECOLOGICOS:Estudios ecol√≥gicos que analizan factores de riesgo poblacionales y correlaciones entre distintas poblaciones.ESTUDIOS DE CASOS Y CONTROLES:Estudios que comparan dos grupos de individuos, uno con la enfermedad de inter√©s y otro sano, para determinar la frecuencia de exposici√≥n a factores de riesgo.CASOS:Casos refers to individuals with the disease of interest in the context of case-control studies.CONTROLES:Controles refers to healthy individuals used as a comparison group in case-control studies.SESGO:Sesgo refers to biases that can affect the validity of case-control studies, particularly in the selection of participants and information gathering.MEMORIA:Memoria refers to the recollection of past exposures by participants, which can influence the accuracy of data in case-control studies.LUCAS ET AL:Lucas et al is a group of researchers who conducted a study comparing pancreatic cancer patients and healthy subjects to assess dietary risk factors.THAO-SALUD INFANTIL:THAO-SALUD INFANTIL is a national program in Spain aimed at promoting healthy lifestyle habits and understanding their impact on obesity development in the study population.PROYECTO PREDIMED:El Proyecto PREDIMED es un ensayo cl√≠nico importante realizado en Espa√±a que estudi√≥ el papel de la dieta mediterr√°nea en la enfermedad cardiovascular en sujetos inicialmente sanos.COMIT√âS √âTICOS DE INVESTIGACI√ìN CL√çNICA:Los Comit√©s √âticos de Investigaci√≥n Cl√≠nica son entidades que revisan y aprueban los protocolos de investigaci√≥n para asegurar que se cumplan los est√°ndares √©ticos y de seguridad en los ensayos cl√≠nicos.INVESTIGACI√ìN B√ÅSICA:La investigaci√≥n b√°sica es un tipo de estudio que busca entender los mecanismos fundamentales de las enfermedades y la biolog√≠a, proporcionando la base para el desarrollo de nuevas terapias.INVESTIGACI√ìN EPIDEMIOL√ìGICA:La investigaci√≥n epidemiol√≥gica se centra en el estudio de la distribuci√≥n y determinantes de la salud y enfermedades en poblaciones, ayudando a establecer relaciones causales.NUTRIGEN√ìMICA:La nutrigen√≥mica es un campo de estudio que investiga c√≥mo los nutrientes afectan la expresi√≥n gen√©tica y c√≥mo la gen√©tica influye en la respuesta a los nutrientes.REAL DECRETO 1090/2015:Real Decreto 1090/2015 is the legislation that regulates clinical trials with medications in Spain, focusing on ethical and methodological standards for trials.AGENCIA ESPA√ëOLA DE MEDICAMENTOS Y PRODUCTOS SANITARIOS:The Agencia Espa√±ola de Medicamentos y Productos Sanitarios is the Spanish Agency responsible for the regulation and oversight of medications and clinical trials.LEY ORG√ÅNICA 15/1999:Ley Org√°nica 15/1999 is the Spanish law concerning the protection of personal data, ensuring the privacy of individuals involved in clinical trials.DECLARACI√ìN DE HELSINKI:The Declaration of Helsinki outlines ethical principles for medical research involving human subjects, which must be adhered to in clinical trials.ESTUDIOS POSTAUTORIZACI√ìN:Post-authorization studies are observational studies conducted with approved medications to monitor their effects in the general population.REAL DECRETO 577/2013:COMIT√âS DE √âTICA DE LA INVESTIGACI√ìN:Comit√©s de √âtica de la Investigaci√≥n are ethical committees that oversee clinical trials to ensure they meet ethical standards.REGISTRO ESPA√ëOL DE ESTUDIOS CL√çNICOS:Registro Espa√±ol de Estudios Cl√≠nicos is the official registry for clinical studies conducted in Spain, ensuring transparency and compliance with regulations.AGENCIA ESPA√ëOLA DEL MEDICAMENTO:The Agencia Espa√±ola del Medicamento is the Spanish agency tasked with the regulation and oversight of medications and clinical trials. As a regulatory body in Spain, it is responsible for the evaluation and supervision of both medicines and medical devices, ensuring their safety, efficacy, and quality for public health.CIBER:CIBER, which stands for Centros de Investigaci√≥n Biom√©dica en Red, is a consortium in Spain designed to enhance biomedical research and health sciences. It serves as a cooperative research structure that aims to promote and strengthen research and development in health by incorporating new thematic areas and research groups. Through its collaborative approach, CIBER seeks to advance the field of biomedical research and improve health outcomes.ISCIII:The Instituto de Salud Carlos III (ISCIII) is a public research institution in Spain that promotes and finances biomedical research.CIBEROBN:CIBERobn focuses on obesity and nutrition research, aiming to understand mechanisms contributing to obesity and related health issues.RETICS:RETICS, or Redes tem√°ticas de investigaci√≥n cooperativa en salud, are organizational structures established in collaboration with the Instituto de Salud Carlos III (ISCIII). These thematic networks are designed to facilitate cooperative research projects in health across various autonomous communities in Spain. RETICS aim to enhance coordination among research groups within the Spanish National Health System, promoting collaborative efforts to advance health research and improve health outcomes.EPIDEMIOLOG√çA Y SALUD P√öBLICA:CIBEResp is a CIBER center that focuses on epidemiology and public health research in Spain.BIOINGENIER√çA, BIOMATERIALES Y NANOMEDICINA:CIBERbbn is a CIBER center that specializes in bioengineering, biomaterials, and nanomedicine research in Spain.DIABETES Y ENFERMEDADES METAB√ìLICAS:CIBERdem is a CIBER center focused on diabetes and metabolic diseases research in Spain.FISIOPATOLOG√çA DE LA OBESIDAD Y LA NUTRICI√ìN:CIBERobn is a CIBER center that studies the pathophysiology of obesity and nutrition in Spain.SALUD MENTAL:CIBERsam is a CIBER center that focuses on mental health research in Spain.ENFERMEDADES HEP√ÅTICAS Y DIGESTIVAS:INSTITUTO DE SALUD CARLOS III:The Instituto de Salud Carlos III is a public research institution located in Spain, dedicated to advancing health research and innovation. It plays a crucial role in coordinating various health research networks and platforms, fostering scientific collaboration among researchers. Additionally, the institution provides funding for a wide range of health-related projects, further supporting the development and implementation of health technologies. Through its efforts, the Instituto de Salud Carlos III aims to enhance public health and contribute to the scientific community's understanding of health issues.PLATAFORMAS:Las Plataformas de apoyo a la investigaci√≥n en ciencias y tecnolog√≠as de la salud are stable collaborative networks associated with the Instituto de Salud Carlos III, focused on supporting research projects in health sciences and technologies.ACTIVIDADES PREVENTIVAS Y PROMOCI√ìN DE LA SALUD EN ATENCI√ìN PRIMARIA:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing on preventive activities and health promotion in primary care.ENFERMEDADES OCULARES:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing on ocular diseases.ENFERMEDADES RENALES:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, dedicated to renal diseases.ENFERMEDADES TROPICALES:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing on tropical diseases.ENFERMEDADES VASCULARES CEREBRALES (ICTUS):This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, dedicated to cerebrovascular diseases, including strokes.FRAGILIDAD Y ENVEJECIMIENTO:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, concentrating on frailty and aging.ENFERMEDADES REUM√ÅTICAS:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing on rheumatic diseases.REACCIONES ADVERSAS A AL√âRGENOS Y F√ÅRMACOS:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, dedicated to adverse reactions to allergens and drugs.SALUD MATERNO-INFANTIL Y DEL DESARROLLO:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing on maternal-infant health and development.SERVICIOS DE SALUD ORIENTADOS A ENFERMEDADES CR√ìNICAS:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, dedicated to health services oriented towards chronic diseases.SIDA:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing on HIV/AIDS research.TERAPIA CELULAR:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, dedicated to cell therapy research.TRASTORNOS ADICTIVOS:This is one of the 17 thematic research networks under RETICS, focusing on addictive disorders.BIOBANCOS:This is one of the four Platforms supporting research in health sciences, focusing on biobanks for biological samples and data.INNOVACI√ìN EN TECNOLOG√çAS M√âDICAS Y SANITARIAS:This is one of the four Platforms supporting research in health sciences, dedicated to innovation in medical and health technologies.UNIDADES DE INVESTIGACI√ìN CL√çNICA Y ENSAYOS CL√çNICOS:This is one of the four Platforms supporting research in health sciences, focusing on clinical research units and clinical trials.RECURSOS BIOMOLECULARES Y BIOINFORM√ÅTICOS:This is one of the four Platforms supporting research in health sciences, concentrating on biomolecular and bioinformatics resources.)<|COMPLETE|>FUNDACI√ìN DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN:A scientific foundation that provides funding for research projects in the field of endocrinology and nutrition in Spain.FUNDACI√ìN DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA DE NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL:A foundation focused on funding research related to parenteral and enteral nutrition in Spain.FUNDACI√ìN LA CAIXA:A private foundation in Spain that funds various social and scientific projects, including research initiatives.FUNDACI√ìN MAPFRE:A private foundation that supports social, cultural, and scientific projects, including funding for research.INSTITUTO DANONE:A research institute that focuses on nutrition and health, providing funding for various research projects.HORIZON 2020:A European Union funding program for research and innovation that was active from 2014 to 2020.ESTRATEGIA ESPA√ëOLA DE CIENCIA Y TECNOLOG√çA Y DE INNOVACI√ìN 2013-2020:A national strategy in Spain aimed at promoting science, technology, and innovation from 2013 to 2020.PLAN ESTATAL DE INVESTIGACI√ìN CIENT√çFICA Y TECNOL√ìGICA Y DE INNOVACI√ìN 2013-2016:A state plan in Spain that outlines the framework for scientific and technological research and innovation from 2013 to 2016.RETO DE SALUD, CAMBIO DEMOGR√ÅFICO Y BIENESTAR:A specific challenge outlined in the Spanish national strategy focusing on health, demographic change, and well-being, which guides research funding priorities.PROGRAMA DE I+D+I ORIENTADA A LOS RETOS DE LA SOCIEDAD:A research and development program in Spain aimed at addressing societal challenges, including health-related issues.CIENCIAS Y TECNOLOG√çAS DE LA SALUD:A field of research that encompasses various health-related studies and innovations, often funded by national and European programs.CONVOCATORIAS P√öBLICAS:Public calls for research funding that are competitive and can be at local, regional, national, or European levels.CONVOCATORIAS PRIVADAS:Private calls for research funding from foundations and organizations that support scientific research.PROYECTOS DE INVESTIGACI√ìN EN SALUD:"PROYECTOS DE INVESTIGACI√ìN EN SALUD" refers to a series of research initiatives that concentrate on health-related issues. These projects are funded and supported by various programs, including the CIBER (Centro de Investigaci√≥n Biom√©dica en Red), and often receive backing from both national and European funding sources. The primary aim of these research projects is to address and explore significant health challenges, contributing to advancements in medical knowledge and public health.SUBPROGRAMA ESTATAL DE FORTALECIMIENTO INSTITUCIONAL:This subprogram aims to incorporate new thematic areas and groups into the CIBER consortium to enhance its research capabilities.SUBPROGRAMA ESTATAL DE FORMACI√ìN:This subprogram provides funding for the hiring of research personnel in various modalities to support scientific projects.SUBPROGRAMA ESTATAL DE MOVILIDAD:The Subprograma Estatal de Movilidad is designed to facilitate the mobility of health researchers and professionals by providing mobility aids. This initiative aims to enhance collaboration and knowledge exchange among researchers, thereby promoting a more interconnected and effective research environment.ACCION ESTRATEGICA EN SALUD:The Acci√≥n Estrat√©gica en Salud is a program designed to enhance talent and employability within the field of health research and training. This strategic initiative emphasizes the promotion of skills and opportunities in health research through a variety of initiatives and funding opportunities, aiming to foster a robust workforce in the health sector.PROGRAMAS CIENT√çFICOS:Scientific programs developed by CIBER to enhance research capabilities and address strategic health challenges.PERSONAL T√âCNICO:Technical personnel hired to support the execution of research projects within the CIBER framework.PROYECTOS DE DESARROLLO TECNOL√ìGICO EN SALUD:Technological development projects in health aimed at improving healthcare solutions and innovations.ACCIONES COMPLEMENTARIAS DE PROGRAMACI√ìN:Complementary programming actions aimed at fostering international collaboration in research and development.SUBPROGRAMA ESTATAL DE FORMACION:The Subprograma Estatal de Formaci√≥n provides various contracts and training opportunities for predoctoral researchers in health.SUBPROGRAMA ESTATAL DE INCORPORACION:The Subprograma Estatal de Incorporaci√≥n focuses on management contracts in health research for university graduates.INSTITUTO DE INVESTIGACION SANITARIA:The Instituto de Investigaci√≥n Sanitaria (IIS) is an institution dedicated to health research.LEY 17/2001:Ley 17/2001 regulates trademarks in Spain, providing legal protection for brands.LEY 11/86:Ley 11/86 governs patents and utility models in Spain, protecting inventions and industrial processes.LEY 11/1988:Ley 11/1988 provides legal protection for the topographies of semiconductor products in Spain.THOMSON REUTERS:Thomson Reuters is a global information and news company that provides data on scientific journals and their impact factors.CONTRATOS RIO HORTEGA:Contratos R√≠o Hortega are contracts for post-specialization training in health, lasting 2 years.CONTRATOS MIGUEL SERVET:Contratos Miguel Servet are contracts for researchers who obtained their doctorate between 2001 and 2011, with a duration of 5 years for Type I and 3 years for Type II.CONTRATOS JUAN RODES:Contratos Juan Rod√©s are contracts for health professionals who combine clinical work and research, lasting 3 years.AYUDAS A LA FORMACION EN GESTION DE LA INVESTIGACION:Ayudas a la formaci√≥n en gesti√≥n de la investigaci√≥n en salud are aids for university graduates to manage health research, lasting 3 years.AYUDAS PARA LA MOVILIDAD DEL PERSONAL INVESTIGADOR:Ayudas para la movilidad del personal investigador are aids for health researchers to facilitate their mobility for 2 to 6 months.PERSONAL INVESTIGADOR:Personal investigador refers to health professionals and researchers involved in health research projects.CONTRATOS PREDOCTORALES:NUTRICI√ìN Y DIET√âTICA:A field of study and research focusing on nutrition and dietetics, including various scientific publications and conferences.ANNUAL REVIEW OF NUTRITION:Annual Review of Nutrition is a scientific journal that publishes comprehensive reviews on various aspects of nutrition.PROCEEDINGS OF THE NUTRITION SOCIETY:Proceedings of the Nutrition Society publishes research and findings presented at the Nutrition Society's meetings.JOURNAL OF NUTRITIONAL BIOCHEMISTRY:The Journal of Nutritional Biochemistry publishes research on the biochemical aspects of nutrition.(N␀␀␀␀␀␀¿N␀␀␀␀␀␀AO␀␀␀␀␀␀+Q␀␀␀␀␀␀§Q␀␀␀␀␀␀LR␀␀␀␀␀␀«R␀␀␀␀␀␀;S␀␀␀␀␀␀ÀS␀␀␀␀␀␀>T␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬂU␀␀␀␀␀␀iV␀␀␀␀␀␀␀W␀␀␀␀␀␀ëW␀␀␀␀␀␀£W␀␀␀␀␀␀nX␀␀␀␀␀␀˚X␀␀␀␀␀␀£Y␀␀␀␀␀␀GZ␀␀␀␀␀␀ZZ␀␀␀␀␀␀[␀␀␀␀␀␀°[␀␀␀␀␀␀/\␀␀␀␀␀␀õ\␀␀␀␀␀␀"]␀␀␀␀␀␀∂]␀␀␀␀␀␀P^␀␀␀␀␀␀e^␀␀␀␀␀␀Î^␀␀␀␀␀␀F_␀␀␀␀␀␀ö_␀␀␀␀␀␀˙_␀␀␀␀␀␀_`␀␀␀␀␀␀´a␀␀␀␀␀␀b␀␀␀␀␀␀Éb␀␀␀␀␀␀›b␀␀␀␀␀␀zc␀␀␀␀␀␀Ëc␀␀␀␀␀␀kd␀␀␀␀␀␀¯d␀␀␀␀␀␀Æe␀␀␀␀␀␀`f␀␀␀␀␀␀*g␀␀␀␀␀␀Ãg␀␀␀␀␀␀lh␀␀␀␀␀␀i␀␀␀␀␀␀±i␀␀␀␀␀␀Mj␀␀␀␀␀␀k␀␀␀␀␀␀çk␀␀␀␀␀␀5l␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇl␀␀␀␀␀␀Øm␀␀␀␀␀␀Pn␀␀␀␀␀␀o␀␀␀␀␀␀¨o␀␀␀␀␀␀Np␀␀␀␀␀␀Ùp␀␀␀␀␀␀óq␀␀␀␀␀␀™q␀␀␀␀␀␀°r␀␀␀␀␀␀=s␀␀␀␀␀␀]s␀␀␀␀␀␀˝s␀␀␀␀␀␀Üt␀␀␀␀␀␀:u␀␀␀␀␀␀Íu␀␀␀␀␀␀Çv␀␀␀␀␀␀*w␀␀␀␀␀␀Óx␀␀␀␀␀␀Éy␀␀␀␀␀␀*z␀␀␀␀␀␀Êz␀␀␀␀␀␀ì{␀␀␀␀␀␀p|␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ|␀␀␀␀␀␀R}␀␀␀␀␀␀⁄}␀␀␀␀␀␀]~␀␀␀␀␀␀ß~␀␀␀␀␀␀˛~␀␀␀␀␀␀∑Ä␀␀␀␀␀␀AÅ␀␀␀␀␀␀ÕÅ␀␀␀␀␀␀UÇ␀␀␀␀␀␀∆Ç␀␀␀␀␀␀0É␀␀␀␀␀␀ôÉ␀␀␀␀␀␀Ñ␀␀␀␀␀␀nÑ␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇÑ␀␀␀␀␀␀vÖ␀␀␀␀␀␀ıÖ␀␀␀␀␀␀ÖÜ␀␀␀␀␀␀˙Ü␀␀␀␀␀␀tá␀␀␀␀␀␀€á␀␀␀␀␀␀@à␀␀␀␀␀␀úà␀␀␀␀␀␀Ïà␀␀␀␀␀␀Pâ␀␀␀␀␀␀Æâ␀␀␀␀␀␀/ä␀␀␀␀␀␀πä␀␀␀␀␀␀Aã␀␀␀␀␀␀Òã␀␀␀␀␀␀áå␀␀␀␀␀␀ç␀␀␀␀␀␀Øç␀␀␀␀␀␀.é␀␀␀␀␀␀4é␀␀␀␀␀␀∑é␀␀␀␀␀␀àè␀␀␀␀␀␀Aê␀␀␀␀␀␀√ê␀␀␀␀␀␀_ë␀␀␀␀␀␀Äë␀␀␀␀␀␀Sí␀␀␀␀␀␀¨ì␀␀␀␀␀␀Nî␀␀␀␀␀␀ï␀␀␀␀␀␀ï␀␀␀␀␀␀◊ï␀␀␀␀␀␀Éñ␀␀␀␀␀␀*ó␀␀␀␀␀␀·ó␀␀␀␀␀␀åò␀␀␀␀␀␀.ô␀␀␀␀␀␀“ô␀␀␀␀␀␀Éö␀␀␀␀␀␀Hõ␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬁõ␀␀␀␀␀␀îú␀␀␀␀␀␀1ù␀␀␀␀␀␀¿ù␀␀␀␀␀␀_û␀␀␀␀␀␀uû␀␀␀␀␀␀€û␀␀␀␀␀␀<ü␀␀␀␀␀␀õü␀␀␀␀␀␀␀†␀␀␀␀␀␀Q†␀